      "$description": "Text styles for macos, in the system font: SF Pro and SF Pro Rounded. Arabic text renders in SF Arabic and SF Arabic Rounded, which the system selects. lineHeight is a ratio of fontSize; the point value is in $extensions. macOS has no Dynamic Type, so these sizes are fixed; the type-scale files repeat them. Values are Apple points. DTCG dimensions allow only px and rem, so 1 px here means 1 pt (a density-independent point, the unit Figma and SwiftUI both use).",
